 step-by-step sequence of Kafka commands to manage topics, producers, and consumers — from start to end?

🛠️ Prerequisites
Ensure Kafka and Zookeeper are installed and running.

# Start Zookeeper
bin/zookeeper-server-start.sh config/zookeeper.properties

# Start Kafka Broker
bin/kafka-server-start.sh config/server.properties
---------------------

📋 Step-by-Step Kafka Commands

🔹 1. Create a Topic
bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --topic orders --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --partitions 3 --replication-factor 1

🔹 2. List All Topics
bin/kafka-topics.sh --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

🔹 3. Describe a Topic (to check partitions & replication)
bin/kafka-topics.sh --describe --topic orders --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

🔹 4. Start a Kafka Console Producer
bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --broker-list localhost:9092 --topic orders

Then type messages like:
order1
order2

🔹 5. Start a Kafka Console Consumer
bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic orders --from-beginning
This will show all messages from the beginning.

🔹 6. Send Keyed Messages via Console Producer (optional)
bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --broker-list localhost:9092 --topic orders --property "parse.key=true" --property "key.separator=:"
Then type:
orderId1:order placed
orderId2:order dispatched

🔹 7. Delete a Kafka Topic
bin/kafka-topics.sh --delete --topic orders --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
⚠️ Make sure delete.topic.enable=true is set in server.properties.

🧹 Optional (Clean-Up Data)
If you're just testing locally and want to remove Kafka/ZK data:
# Stop Kafka and Zookeeper first
rm -rf /tmp/kafka-logs
rm -rf /tmp/zookeeper

